infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Error idioms by caller coupling
  desc Default to the lowest rung — export a sentinel or type only when a caller must branch on the failure
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Opaque — just return error
      desc Exposes nothing; callers can only log or propagate, so you stay free to change everything behind the message. The senior default.
    - label Sentinel — var ErrX = errors.New(...)
      desc Cheap identity branch via errors.Is, but carries no data and is permanent public API forever.
    - label Typed — struct implements error
      desc Carries fields (path, code) reached with errors.As; richest data, heaviest contract callers couple to.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #6366f1 #f43f5e
